---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";

const updated = "September 9, 2026";
const contactEmail = "robotics-outreach@tawasaw.org";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Tawasaw Robotics"
  description="How Tawasaw Robotics Silicon Valley handles information collected through this website and our program applications."
>
  <main>
    <div class="subnav">
      <div class="shell subnav__inner">
        <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/">
          <Icon name="arrow-left" size={18} />
          Return home
        </a>
        <p class="subnav__season">Last updated {updated}</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell section__inner page-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Tawasaw Robotics runs youth robotics programs in Silicon Valley. Most
          of the families we work with are entrusting us with information about
          their children, so we keep what we collect small and we do not sell
          it — ever.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--muted">
      <div class="shell section__inner">
        <div class="policy">
          <h2>The short version</h2>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li>
              This website sets no cookies and runs no analytics, advertising,
              or tracking scripts.
            </li>
            <li>
              We collect personal information only when you send it to us —
              through a program application form or by email.
            </li>
            <li>
              We never sell or rent personal information, and we do not share it
              for advertising.
            </li>
            <li>
              Applications for our programs are submitted by a parent or
              guardian, and a parent or guardian can ask us to delete them at
              any time.
            </li>
            <li>
              Enrolled families and coaches also use a separate sign-in-only
              portal, which does keep accounts and records. It is described in
              its own section below.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            This site is operated by Tawasaw Robotics.
          </p>
          <p>
            This policy covers two things: this public website,
            <strong>robotics.tawasaw.org</strong>, together with the program
            applications linked from it; and the program portal at
            <strong>robotics.tawasaw.com</strong>, which enrolled families and
            coaches sign in to. They are separate systems and they handle
            information differently, so each is described separately below.
          </p>
          <p>
            It does not cover other Tawasaw Institute websites, or the
            third-party sites and services described below, each of which has
            its own privacy policy.
          </p>

          <h2>Information we collect</h2>

          <h3>Information you give us</h3>
          <p>
            Our application pages embed a Google Form. When a parent or guardian
            completes one, the form collects the information requested on it —
            typically the student's name, age or grade, school, program of
            interest, and a parent or guardian's name, email address, and phone
            number, along with anything else you choose to write in.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you
            include in your message.
          </p>

          <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>This public website</strong> is static. It has no accounts,
            no logins, and no database of visitors. We do not set cookies here,
            and we do not use Google Analytics or any other analytics or
            advertising service.
          </p>
          <p>
            The portal at robotics.tawasaw.com is different — it has accounts
            and it does keep records. See <a href="#portal">The program portal</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Two services do see technical information simply because the site
            loads through them:
          </p>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>
              <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> hosts this site and records standard
              server request information, such as IP addresses, for security and
              operations. We do not have access to those logs.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Google Fonts</strong> serves the typefaces used here.
              Loading a page requests those font files from Google's servers,
              which means Google receives your IP address and browser
              information as part of that request.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2 id="portal">The program portal</h2>
          <p>
            Once a student has a place on a team, we run the season through our
            own application at <strong>robotics.tawasaw.com</strong>. Unlike this
            public website, it has accounts and it keeps records.
          </p>

          <h3>Who has an account</h3>
          <p>
            Only people we have already added: enrolled students, their parents
            and guardians, and the coaches, mentors and administrators who run
            the program. <strong>There is no public sign-up.</strong> If someone
            we have not added tries to sign in, the portal turns them away
            rather than creating an account. This is a program for children, and
            an open sign-up would put strangers inside the family roster.
          </p>

          <h3>How signing in works</h3>
          <p>
            There are no passwords, so there is no password for us to store or
            for anyone to steal. You sign in one of two ways:
          </p>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>
              <strong>With Google.</strong> We ask Google only for your name,
              email address, and profile picture. We cannot read or send your
              mail, and we cannot see your contacts, calendar, files, or
              anything else in your Google account. Google confirms you control
              the address; we never see your Google password.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>With a one-time link</strong> emailed to the address we
              already hold for you. The link expires after five minutes, is
              stored only as a cryptographic hash, and works once.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Signing in sets a session cookie so you stay signed in for up to
            thirty days. It exists only to keep you signed in — it does not
            track you, and there are no advertising or analytics cookies
            anywhere in the portal.
          </p>

          <h3>What the portal stores</h3>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>
              <strong>People and households</strong> — name, email address,
              phone number, and which family a person belongs to.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Team membership</strong> — which team someone is on, in
              what role, and when they joined or left.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Applications</strong> — a student's application for a
              season and the decision on it, including any note an administrator
              recorded.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Signed agreements</strong> — which agreement a guardian
              signed, for which student, and when.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Attendance</strong> — arrival and departure times at team
              meetings, and whether an absence was excused.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>An audit log</strong> — a record of administrative
              actions, so a change to a child's record can always be traced to
              the adult who made it.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We do not currently use camera check-in, so no QR badge is issued
            and no photograph is taken at check-in.
          </p>

          <h3>Where it runs</h3>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>
              <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the portal and stores its
              database. Cloudflare processes this information on our behalf.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Resend</strong> delivers the portal's email — sign-in
              links and notices about an application.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Zeffy</strong> is the platform donations are made through.
              The portal mirrors what Zeffy reports about a donation so we can
              keep our own books. It no longer links a donation to a person or a
              household record, and our program charges no registration fee.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Deleting a portal record</h3>
          <p>
            A parent or guardian can ask us to erase their family's records,
            either by email or from within the portal, and an administrator
            reviews the request.
          </p>
          <p>
            Completing an erasure removes contact details, the sign-in account
            and any pending sign-in link, badge tokens, the original imported
            spreadsheet row, and the free-text reason on any excused absence.
          </p>
          <p>
            Some things are kept, and we would rather say so plainly than imply
            otherwise. A signed agreement, an attendance record, a donation
            record and the audit log remain, because a minor's signed agreement
            may need to outlive their reaching adulthood, and donation records
            are kept for seven years for accounting. A person's name is kept so
            those remaining records stay attributable. The record is archived
            rather than deleted outright, and it is closed to everyone,
            including the guardian who could previously see it.
          </p>

          <h2>How we use information</h2>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>To review applications and place students into a team.</li>
            <li>
              To contact families about meetings, schedule changes, competitions,
              travel, permission forms, and other program logistics.
            </li>
            <li>To answer questions you send us.</li>
            <li>
              To keep basic records of team rosters and season participation.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We do not use your information to build advertising profiles, and we
            do not use it for any purpose unrelated to running the program.
          </p>

          <h2>Third-party services we rely on</h2>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>
              <strong>Google Workspace</strong> — Google Forms collects
              applications, and the responses are stored in our Google account
              along with our program email.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Google Sign-In</strong> — one of the two ways to sign in
              to the portal. We receive only your name, email address, and
              profile picture.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosting and the database behind the
              program portal.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Resend</strong> — delivers the portal's sign-in links and
              notices.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Zeffy</strong> — the donation platform, and the source of
              what the portal shows about a donation.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> — website hosting.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Google Fonts</strong> — web typefaces.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Instagram and YouTube</strong> — our social accounts.
              Following those links takes you to Meta and Google properties,
              which track visitors under their own policies.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>FIRST</strong> — students who compete must be registered
              with FIRST by a parent or guardian through the FIRST registration
              system. That registration, including the consent and release forms
              it requires, is handled directly by FIRST under its own privacy
              policy.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Who we share information with</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>We do not sell, rent, or trade personal information.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>We share it only in these situations:</p>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>
              With coaches, mentors, and staff who need it to run the program.
            </li>
            <li>
              With the service providers listed above, which process information
              on our behalf.
            </li>
            <li>
              With FIRST and tournament organizers when a team registers for or
              competes at an event, as those events require.
            </li>
            <li>
              When the law requires it, or when it is necessary to protect the
              safety of a participant.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Our programs serve students from roughly ages 9 through 18, so we
            expect to handle information about children. We ask that
            applications and other correspondence about a student come from a
            parent or guardian, not from the student directly.
          </p>
          <p>
            We collect the minimum needed to run the program safely, we do not
            knowingly collect personal information from a child under 13 without
            a parent or guardian, and we do not use children's information for
            advertising or share it for marketing purposes.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you believe a child has sent us personal information without a
            parent's or guardian's involvement, email us and we will delete it.
          </p>

          <h2>Photos and video</h2>
          <p>
            We sometimes photograph or record team activities and competitions
            and share highlights on our Instagram and YouTube accounts or on
            this website. Media consent is handled through the FIRST
            registration and consent forms and through our own
            permission forms. If you would prefer that your child not appear in
            photos or video we publish, tell us and we will honor that — and if
            something is already posted, contact us and we will take it down.
          </p>

          <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
          <p>
            We keep application responses and roster information for as long as
            a student participates, plus a reasonable period afterward for
            season records and to make it easy for returning families to sign
            up again. Email correspondence is kept in our program mailbox. You
            can ask us to delete a record sooner.
          </p>
          <p>
            Portal records follow the same principle, with two exceptions we
            keep deliberately: a signed agreement, because a minor's consent may
            need to outlive their reaching adulthood, and a donation record,
            kept seven years for accounting. What an erasure removes and what it
            keeps is set out under
            <a href="#portal">Deleting a portal record</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>Security</h2>
          <p>
            Applications and email live in access-controlled Google accounts
            limited to the adults who run the program, and this site is served
            over HTTPS. No method of storage or transmission is perfectly
            secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security, but we limit both
            what we collect and who can see it.
          </p>
          <p>
            The portal is served over HTTPS and stores no passwords, so there is
            no password to be lost in a breach. What each person can see is
            decided for every request rather than by what the screen happens to
            show: a coach reaches their own team, a guardian reaches their own
            family, and a student reaches only their own attendance. Guardian
            contact details follow responsibility for a team, not the running of
            its attendance, so an adult who only takes the register does not see
            them.
          </p>

          <h2>Your choices and requests</h2>
          <p>
            Email us at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> to:
          </p>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>Ask what information we hold about you or your child.</li>
            <li>Correct information that is wrong or out of date.</li>
            <li>Ask us to delete an application or other records.</li>
            <li>
              Ask us to erase your family's portal records — you can also raise
              this from inside the portal itself.
            </li>
            <li>Ask us to stop contacting you.</li>
            <li>Ask us to remove a photo or video.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            California residents, including parents acting for their children,
            have rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act to know,
            delete, and correct personal information, and not to be
            discriminated against for exercising them. We do not sell or share
            personal information as those terms are defined by the CCPA. Send
            any request to the address above and we will respond.
          </p>

          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            If we change how we handle information, we will update this page and
            the "last updated" date at the top. Material changes affecting
            current families will also go out by email.
          </p>

          <h2>Contact us</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about this policy or about your family's information:
            <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="policy__updated">Last updated {updated}.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
